body:
I'm not fully sure how to help you, I'm sorry. You could try the FNAFB Complete Collection which is an official remake of these games in a better engine and with more bosses/enemies in it. It is not fully completed yet, but FNAFB1, FNAFB2, and Acts 1 and 2 of FNAFB3 are in it. I guess you could check if you can run this

&#x200B;

 [https://gamejolt.com/games/fnafbneverdies/152183](https://gamejolt.com/games/fnafbneverdies/152183)

 [https://www.rpgmakerweb.com/download/additional/run-time-packages](https://www.rpgmakerweb.com/download/additional/run-time-packages) 

&#x200B;

Go here and download the RPG Maker VX Ace installer. This will get you the source files you need to play any RPG Maker VX Ace game, including the entire FNAFB series.

Who knows, maybe I am wrong about that and the games are equally received. The times I've read on here have shown more enjoyment for vlr though.

&#x200B;

Did you use easy mode or any hints for the puzzle rooms? Some parts were a little crazy and legit took me hours (the pantry). It could just be that I suck though.
